WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.757 --> 00:00:06.497
The internet has changed the way we live.

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:09.419
It has changed the way we work,

00:00:09.919 --> 00:00:10.700
the way we shop,

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.720
and even the way we date.

00:00:13.541 --> 00:00:16.361
It has also changed the way we kill.

00:00:17.961 --> 00:00:19.163
I'm Donald McIntyre,

00:00:19.262 --> 00:00:23.603
and I'm on a quest to explore the dark side of our online world,

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.184
where one click can lead to murder.

00:00:27.765 --> 00:00:28.385
The internet is...

00:00:28.405 --> 00:00:31.410
social media has been a godsend to online predators.

00:00:31.589 --> 00:00:31.829
Why?

00:00:31.869 --> 00:00:33.993
Because of the speed in which they can one,

00:00:34.292 --> 00:00:35.393
create fake profiles,

00:00:35.454 --> 00:00:35.854
but two,

00:00:35.954 --> 00:00:36.816
access victims.

00:00:37.656 --> 00:00:41.682
I'll be investigating some of the most disturbing crimes in recent history,

00:00:42.222 --> 00:00:43.183
where the internet and...

00:00:43.384 --> 00:00:45.346
social media have been used to trick,

00:00:45.686 --> 00:00:47.887
torture and kill innocent victims,

00:00:48.207 --> 00:00:51.670
lured into a virtual world where nothing is as it seems.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:52.551
Clearly,

00:00:52.631 --> 00:00:57.314
she did not realise the person she was talking to online was the man who was going to kill her.

00:00:59.057 --> 00:01:00.817
In this programme,

00:01:00.878 --> 00:01:05.542
15-year-old A-star student Joshua Davies seemed the perfect boyfriend for

00:01:06.042 --> 00:01:07.302
14-year-old Rebecca Aylward.

00:01:07.963 --> 00:01:08.844
But when When they broke up,

00:01:09.125 --> 00:01:11.266
he waged a 10-month online war,

00:01:11.587 --> 00:01:13.128
which ended with him brutally killing

00:01:13.408 --> 00:01:15.009
murdering his ex-girlfriend.

00:01:18.071 --> 00:01:21.953
When Davies told his friends online that he was going to kill Rebecca,

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:23.995
they didn't think he was serious.

00:01:24.295 --> 00:01:25.436
They even egged him on.

00:01:25.936 --> 00:01:30.479
Are we now in a world where teenagers can't draw a line between fiction and reality?

00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:36.723
A world where social media can help a youngster talk himself into committing a brutal murder.

00:02:14.823 --> 00:02:17.685
These days when teenagers meet and get together at school,

00:02:18.044 --> 00:02:21.448
increasingly they're conducting their relationships online,

00:02:21.848 --> 00:02:29.074
with sites like Facebook being used to keep their peers updated about how the relationship is going 24-7.

00:02:31.024 --> 00:02:33.066
This was the case with year 10 students

00:02:33.406 --> 00:02:35.668
Joshua Davies and Rebecca Aylward.

00:02:36.269 --> 00:02:38.430
They had an intense but brief relationship,

00:02:38.971 --> 00:02:39.871
and when they broke up,

00:02:40.311 --> 00:02:42.573
Davies was determined to save face.

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:45.795
He made no secret of his hatred for Rebecca,

00:02:46.356 --> 00:02:49.218
and nearly 14 months after they started dating,

00:02:49.639 --> 00:02:50.180
on October

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:51.800
23rd, 2010,

00:02:52.341 --> 00:02:55.243
he took her to a forest and murdered her.

00:03:20.807 --> 00:03:29.353
I'm on my way to Abercanvig near Bridgend in Wales where Joshua Davies lived and where Rebecca Aylward was murdered in 2010.

00:03:29.774 --> 00:03:38.799
And I want to discover the role social media played in transforming a seemingly model student into a brutal and callous killer.

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:49.868
Like most teenage girls,

00:03:50.149 --> 00:03:50.549
Rebecca,

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.951
known as Becca to her friends and family,

00:03:53.291 --> 00:03:55.292
was into social media and boys.

00:03:55.973 --> 00:04:00.776
She was a bright girl with a wide circle of friends and dreamed of becoming a lawyer.

00:04:02.832 --> 00:04:03.052
To me,

00:04:03.072 --> 00:04:03.953
Becca was my best friend.

00:04:04.393 --> 00:04:05.334
When I first met Becca,

00:04:05.493 --> 00:04:09.076
I thought she was really confident,

00:04:09.116 --> 00:04:09.475
I thought.

00:04:09.897 --> 00:04:16.161
Definitely seemed far smarter than the rest of understanding themselves and what they want in life and things like that.

00:04:16.181 --> 00:04:18.521
She already had goals of where she wanted to be in life,

00:04:18.523 --> 00:04:20.223
and I was enamoured of her,

00:04:20.223 --> 00:04:21.744
which was awesome.

00:04:21.745 --> 00:04:25.927
Author Lynn Barrett-Lee co-wrote a book about Becca with Becca's mother,

00:04:26.067 --> 00:04:26.427
Sonia.

00:04:27.411 --> 00:04:29.072
From everything I've read about Becca,

00:04:31.012 --> 00:04:35.673
she's just come across throughout as being just a fabulous older sister.

00:04:35.853 --> 00:04:37.194
Very maternal,

00:04:37.274 --> 00:04:38.034
like a little mum.

00:04:38.854 --> 00:04:40.275
She worked hard at school,

00:04:40.455 --> 00:04:41.755
she had big ambitions,

00:04:41.756 --> 00:04:42.815
she wanted to be a lawyer,

00:04:43.697 --> 00:04:45.236
so just a lovely daughter.

00:04:45.836 --> 00:04:46.376
She was great,

00:04:46.477 --> 00:04:49.517
like really protective of her friends.

00:04:50.278 --> 00:04:51.518
A really loving person.

00:04:52.399 --> 00:04:52.558
Yeah,

00:04:52.738 --> 00:04:53.739
she was something special.

00:04:58.637 --> 00:04:59.979
Rebecca and Joshua met at the-

00:05:00.139 --> 00:05:03.723
Secondary school here where they enjoyed the same large group of friends,

00:05:03.963 --> 00:05:06.485
but they didn't start dating until their GCSE year.

00:05:07.165 --> 00:05:10.848
Now Joshua was regarded as academically gifted and a charming boy.

00:05:11.307 --> 00:05:13.309
Even Rebecca's mother thought highly of him.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:17.351
She said of him that even though he towered above her and Rebecca,

00:05:17.812 --> 00:05:20.615
he had a round baby face and was soft-natured.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.181
If a mock back had told me of him,

00:05:28.921 --> 00:05:29.081
yeah,

00:05:29.502 --> 00:05:30.122
great student,

00:05:30.662 --> 00:05:31.643
normal 15-year-old kid.

00:05:31.823 --> 00:05:32.864
Everyone just thought he was cool.

00:05:33.204 --> 00:05:34.745
He seemed like a really genuinely nice guy.

00:05:35.586 --> 00:05:39.348
He was the life and soul of many parties or even the classroom.

00:05:40.169 --> 00:05:42.050
It wasn't difficult for him to make friends.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:43.290
He played rugby.

00:05:43.951 --> 00:05:49.173
He was thought of as the charming young man that every girl would want to go out with.

00:05:49.953 --> 00:05:50.614
Good-looking,

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:53.735
by all accounts very charismatic.

00:05:54.014 --> 00:05:59.097
The sort of boy who had a sort of coterie of other boys around him that sort of gathered people to him,

00:05:59.157 --> 00:06:00.177
very much top dog.

00:06:00.179 --> 00:06:00.398
I mean,

00:06:00.399 --> 00:06:01.817
I think he called himself that once.

00:06:02.398 --> 00:06:03.098
I'm top dog.

00:06:03.179 --> 00:06:04.098
That was his big thing.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:13.036
When Becca and Davies started dating in September 2009,

00:06:13.038 --> 00:06:17.540
Becca's family were delighted that she'd found such a nice young man who seemed to make her happy.

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:20.081
According to friends and family,

00:06:20.401 --> 00:06:21.682
they were besotted with each other.

00:06:23.403 --> 00:06:27.387
Rebecca and Davis had the classic teenager relationship for the time.

00:06:27.466 --> 00:06:29.769
The fact that they would see each other at school,

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:32.011
see each other a bit after school,

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.733
and then want to talk the minute they got home on social media.

00:06:34.893 --> 00:06:38.396
So they would have 24-7 contact with each other.

00:06:38.496 --> 00:06:39.297
But at the time,

00:06:39.317 --> 00:06:40.377
and even today,

00:06:40.798 --> 00:06:42.079
that is something that teenagers do.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:44.199
Clearly,

00:06:44.259 --> 00:06:45.120
he made her happy.

00:06:45.721 --> 00:06:46.901
And she was very,

00:06:47.002 --> 00:06:47.322
very,

00:06:47.822 --> 00:06:48.362
I would say,

00:06:48.422 --> 00:06:49.442
very much in love.

00:06:49.882 --> 00:06:52.564
He'd spend evenings having dinner at their house,

00:06:52.625 --> 00:06:53.525
weekends with them.

00:06:54.925 --> 00:06:56.206
He made comments to

00:06:56.607 --> 00:07:00.569
Rebecca's mom that he would look after her and take care of her and that she was safe with him.

00:07:01.049 --> 00:07:02.129
For all intents and purposes,

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.329
it seemed quite a healthy,

00:07:03.509 --> 00:07:03.831
normal,

00:07:03.891 --> 00:07:04.811
loving relationship.

00:07:08.508 --> 00:07:08.748
However,

00:07:08.808 --> 00:07:13.271
I think there's some slight indications of his controlling nature.

00:07:13.771 --> 00:07:16.252
The fact that he said things like,

00:07:16.693 --> 00:07:17.873
I will take care of her,

00:07:18.293 --> 00:07:19.234
she's safe with me,

00:07:19.774 --> 00:07:21.595
almost like he was the one in power.

00:07:23.192 --> 00:07:25.874
There was more to Joshua Davies than met the eye.

00:07:26.254 --> 00:07:28.175
His friend spoke of his need to be the leader,

00:07:28.456 --> 00:07:30.038
the one that everyone followed.

00:07:30.619 --> 00:07:34.081
He would quickly turn on those who said anything negative about him,

00:07:34.542 --> 00:07:38.906
happily voicing his aggression on social media or here at school,

00:07:39.286 --> 00:07:40.007
face to face.

00:07:47.456 --> 00:07:50.596
Joshua was a lad who found it very,

00:07:50.656 --> 00:07:53.057
very difficult to accept any kind of challenge.

00:07:54.158 --> 00:07:57.940
And he certainly didn't like any kind of rejection at all.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:00.742
And his friends said this kind of thing about him.

00:08:00.742 --> 00:08:01.361
He was all right,

00:08:01.362 --> 00:08:02.041
he was fine,

00:08:02.483 --> 00:08:04.523
until you somehow annoyed him.

00:08:04.743 --> 00:08:05.764
And then he would just,

00:08:06.324 --> 00:08:06.563
you know,

00:08:06.743 --> 00:08:08.024
change into a different person.

00:08:09.445 --> 00:08:13.666
People like Joshua aren't necessarily routinely violent.

00:08:14.567 --> 00:08:14.908
but what

00:08:15.163 --> 00:08:16.243
What does tend to happen,

00:08:16.824 --> 00:08:18.865
especially when they have some kind of rejection,

00:08:19.384 --> 00:08:29.207
is that a rage or a sense of entitlement builds up inside them and it's that that can make them become violent.

00:08:30.247 --> 00:08:32.468
It's very similar to many narcissists.

00:08:32.668 --> 00:08:35.330
They don't take personal criticism very well.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:43.771
They will ice people who they think have belittled them and cut them out of their lives and they will often bear grudges and vendettas against people.

00:08:44.288 --> 00:08:47.328
for the most innocuous of perceived slights.

00:08:51.149 --> 00:08:52.169
Ominously for Becca,

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:54.471
she would soon become the focus of Davies'

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:54.831
anger.

00:08:57.371 --> 00:08:59.111
Three months into their relationship,

00:08:59.591 --> 00:09:02.452
during the Christmas holidays of 2009,

00:09:02.453 --> 00:09:04.713
Davies broke up with Becca unexpectedly.

00:09:05.453 --> 00:09:06.473
She was devastated.

00:09:07.793 --> 00:09:10.075
Becca was shocked beyond belief.

00:09:10.154 --> 00:09:13.436
She did not have any idea why he'd finished with her.

00:09:17.908 --> 00:09:20.289
Everything had been going well as far as she was concerned.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.431
They were happy together.

00:09:22.211 --> 00:09:22.912
And then suddenly,

00:09:22.971 --> 00:09:23.533
out of the blue,

00:09:23.913 --> 00:09:25.134
he didn't want to be with her anymore.

00:09:26.134 --> 00:09:26.375
You know,

00:09:26.375 --> 00:09:29.878
it's bad enough when somebody finishes with you when you know things are going wrong,

00:09:29.937 --> 00:09:32.539
but it just came out of the blue and she didn't understand.

00:09:33.941 --> 00:09:35.241
It was also a difficult time.

00:09:35.361 --> 00:09:37.244
Her parents had recently divorced,

00:09:37.864 --> 00:09:39.826
so she would have been feeling particularly vulnerable.

00:09:40.265 --> 00:09:41.067
Every teenager,

00:09:41.086 --> 00:09:42.947
when they have that first relationship,

00:09:42.967 --> 00:09:44.288
it's really overpowering.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:45.971
They spent all their time together.

00:09:46.051 --> 00:09:47.251
He was her best friend.

00:09:47.668 --> 00:09:48.808
as well as her boyfriend.

00:09:49.889 --> 00:09:51.110
From that moment on,

00:09:52.012 --> 00:09:54.294
it was almost as if she became public enemy number one.

00:09:55.816 --> 00:09:56.036
You know,

00:09:56.037 --> 00:09:58.578
as far as Davis and his friends were concerned,

00:09:59.078 --> 00:09:59.980
she'd suddenly gone...

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:03.743
From being his girlfriend to being in some sort of enemy camp.

00:10:07.566 --> 00:10:12.109
This is where the other side of social media really hits because if you break up,

00:10:12.208 --> 00:10:20.735
in this situation Rebecca would not only see him at school but see him in the small town that they lived in but also see activity online to know what he's doing,

00:10:20.754 --> 00:10:21.556
what he's posting,

00:10:21.895 --> 00:10:22.657
what he's saying.

00:10:23.057 --> 00:10:27.320
Now whether that's nasty or not she'd be able to see that and that just adds to the pain.

00:10:35.096 --> 00:10:39.157
Josh's cruel and vindictive streak began to surface soon after the breakup.

00:10:39.617 --> 00:10:48.340
He announced here at school and on social media that he broke up with Rebecca because she was a slag in his words and was trying to get pregnant with his kid.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:49.940
But Rebecca would have none of it.

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:55.562
She defended herself robustly from his bullying and refused to let him have the last word.

00:10:56.042 --> 00:10:57.242
And he hated her for it.

00:11:11.076 --> 00:11:14.477
I've come to Abercanvig in Wales to investigate why,

00:11:14.538 --> 00:11:15.739
in 2010,

00:11:16.198 --> 00:11:21.442
Joshua Davies lured his ex-girlfriend Becca into a forest and then brutally killed her.

00:11:22.222 --> 00:11:25.944
I want to find out the role social media played in this horrific murder.

00:11:27.805 --> 00:11:28.807
This is a photograph of

00:11:29.226 --> 00:11:35.530
15-year-old Becca Aylward and her boyfriend Joshua Davies before they broke up in Christmas 2009.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:37.491
And few could have anticipated...

00:11:37.879 --> 00:11:40.902
The anger and resentment that this breakup would generate.

00:11:41.702 --> 00:11:41.963
Josh,

00:11:42.023 --> 00:11:42.203
though,

00:11:42.243 --> 00:11:47.808
was always determined to have the last word and took to social media to vent his feelings about Becca.

00:11:48.508 --> 00:11:49.089
Tragically,

00:11:49.169 --> 00:11:49.389
though,

00:11:49.849 --> 00:11:53.993
his actions would not be confined just to the online world.

00:12:04.062 --> 00:12:05.203
There were many issues...

00:12:05.864 --> 00:12:09.586
surrounding social media and the risks and dangers it poses,

00:12:09.666 --> 00:12:12.908
one of which we always know is cyberbullying or online bullying.

00:12:13.368 --> 00:12:13.528
Now,

00:12:13.628 --> 00:12:15.609
Davis knows what he can say on social media.

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:17.509
He can turn people against Rebecca.

00:12:17.769 --> 00:12:20.572
Maybe that deep down he wanted Rebecca back,

00:12:20.612 --> 00:12:21.012
so he thought,

00:12:21.013 --> 00:12:21.112
well,

00:12:21.113 --> 00:12:21.833
if I upset her,

00:12:21.893 --> 00:12:22.653
she's got to come to me.

00:12:22.713 --> 00:12:24.114
I'm the only person that's going to talk to her.

00:12:24.894 --> 00:12:25.754
That is control.

00:12:26.315 --> 00:12:29.976
And this is your classic bully tactics by using social media,

00:12:29.978 --> 00:12:32.758
because social media affords this 24-7.

00:12:32.798 --> 00:12:35.580
He was trying to make it as difficult as he could.

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:42.906
and would make up things about her and try and spread rumours about her so that other people would turn against her.

00:12:43.046 --> 00:12:44.586
It wasn't enough that he hated her.

00:12:44.706 --> 00:12:46.849
He had to make sure everybody else hated her as well.

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:52.933
Rumours about Becca that I knew of were related to pregnancy,

00:12:53.454 --> 00:12:55.355
and also it was made up that she'd had,

00:12:55.436 --> 00:12:55.656
like,

00:12:55.735 --> 00:12:56.976
loads and loads of partners,

00:12:57.336 --> 00:12:59.079
her friendships with people as well.

00:12:59.778 --> 00:13:02.581
By saying she said different things about people that she hadn't said,

00:13:03.101 --> 00:13:03.282
really,

00:13:03.322 --> 00:13:03.502
like,

00:13:03.643 --> 00:13:04.903
just tore her away from her.

00:13:04.904 --> 00:13:05.344
away from her

00:13:05.423 --> 00:13:05.783
friends.

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:15.713
When they went back to school after the Christmas holidays,

00:13:16.134 --> 00:13:20.217
Davies continued to try and persuade other students not to speak to Becca.

00:13:21.178 --> 00:13:22.039
But after school,

00:13:22.259 --> 00:13:25.842
he used private messages online to be friendly towards her.

00:13:26.903 --> 00:13:29.307
It was a masterclass in manipulation.

00:13:30.648 --> 00:13:33.071
They would talk a lot on MSN.

00:13:33.151 --> 00:13:35.533
She'd send me screenshots of their conversations.

00:13:35.814 --> 00:13:36.594
And a lot of the time,

00:13:36.955 --> 00:13:39.357
they'd come up and actually have a genuinely really nice conversation.

00:13:39.498 --> 00:13:39.677
Like,

00:13:39.718 --> 00:13:40.939
he was so on and off with her,

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:42.921
and she always did quite like him.

00:13:43.762 --> 00:13:46.565
It seems that they had an ongoing relationship,

00:13:46.705 --> 00:13:48.466
even though they weren't in a relationship.

00:13:49.559 --> 00:13:51.881
We have something called the push-pull effect in psychology,

00:13:52.761 --> 00:13:56.985
and it's used very much in domestic abuse and also grooming of people,

00:13:57.325 --> 00:14:02.668
that you pull them in with lots of emotion and love and adoration,

00:14:03.109 --> 00:14:04.429
and then you push them away.

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:07.291
with some cruel words or ending the relationship,

00:14:07.591 --> 00:14:08.831
and then you pull them back again.

00:14:09.131 --> 00:14:10.311
And the more you do that,

00:14:10.531 --> 00:14:11.972
the more you're messing with their head,

00:14:12.252 --> 00:14:14.172
and the more you're actually tying them in with you,

00:14:14.232 --> 00:14:15.873
you're emotionally attaching them to you,

00:14:16.293 --> 00:14:19.773
because they're so confused by it that they're actually wanting you more.

00:14:20.274 --> 00:14:22.533
And I think because she was so young,

00:14:23.054 --> 00:14:24.595
and this was her first relationship,

00:14:24.596 --> 00:14:26.875
and of course she doesn't have any experience with relationships,

00:14:27.275 --> 00:14:29.876
I think that actually made her want him more.

00:14:35.036 --> 00:14:36.477
In spring 2010,

00:14:36.778 --> 00:14:38.799
despite being friendly to Becca in private,

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:39.620
in public,

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:41.922
Davies continued his war of words.

00:14:44.444 --> 00:14:48.308
And his barrage of hatred started to become even more extreme.

00:14:49.789 --> 00:14:52.912
So Becca stood up to Davies and defended her name.

00:14:53.573 --> 00:14:55.314
It led to a furious response.

00:14:57.847 --> 00:14:58.327
For Davies,

00:14:58.329 --> 00:14:59.749
that was probably something quite new,

00:14:59.808 --> 00:15:01.249
this person challenging him,

00:15:01.349 --> 00:15:05.230
this person publicly challenging his version of events,

00:15:05.291 --> 00:15:07.412
his truth that he wanted everyone to believe.

00:15:07.851 --> 00:15:10.332
And because of his narcissistic temperament,

00:15:10.653 --> 00:15:14.575
he could not cope with people publicly contradicting him.

00:15:14.654 --> 00:15:15.475
That would not do.

00:15:16.555 --> 00:15:17.596
During the summer term...

00:15:18.004 --> 00:15:22.145
Davies intensified his efforts to demoralize Becca on social media.

00:15:22.966 --> 00:15:27.707
And soon he advanced from insults to explicit threats to physically harm her.

00:15:28.788 --> 00:15:33.430
That shows that he was having to escalate things because he could no longer contain

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:37.651
Rebecca and the risk to his reputation that she posed online,

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:40.111
and he had to take those threats into the real world.

00:15:56.883 --> 00:15:57.043
Well,

00:15:57.063 --> 00:16:03.545
we know from the online chat histories and statements revealed by the police that far from fizzling out,

00:16:03.905 --> 00:16:06.987
the anger and resentment between the pair began to escalate,

00:16:07.367 --> 00:16:08.427
and in Josh's case,

00:16:08.707 --> 00:16:09.828
to disturbing levels.

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:15.950
Clearly,

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:20.251
what was going on online between them was one thing,

00:16:20.791 --> 00:16:23.252
but there was obviously at the same time,

00:16:23.253 --> 00:16:24.432
or very soon after,

00:16:25.352 --> 00:16:26.953
a much darker thing emerging,

00:16:27.193 --> 00:16:30.774
and that's what we now know was going on between him and his friends,

00:16:30.834 --> 00:16:34.695
that he'd started thinking about ways he could kill her.

00:16:40.428 --> 00:16:47.276
He occasionally would pepper his continual dialogue of I'm going to kill her with methods and how it would be done.

00:16:48.978 --> 00:16:53.202
He talked about pushing her off the edge of a quarry so she'd drown.

00:16:53.943 --> 00:16:57.507
He talked about poisoning her at some length.

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:05.305
These seem so fanciful and outrageous that I think his peer group didn't pay them any notice.

00:17:05.985 --> 00:17:08.107
Because surely if you're going to kill someone,

00:17:08.288 --> 00:17:11.110
you don't keep talking about it and incriminating yourself.

00:17:12.732 --> 00:17:16.616
He's got the idea in his head that he is going to kill her.

00:17:17.457 --> 00:17:24.363
And the fact that he's talking about different methods of killing her indicate that it's the killing her that is the important thing.

00:17:25.124 --> 00:17:26.825
He wants to enjoy doing it.

00:17:27.405 --> 00:17:29.406
He doesn't want her to be killed by somebody else.

00:17:29.446 --> 00:17:30.666
He wants to be there.

00:17:31.046 --> 00:17:34.107
He wants to be master of that.

00:17:34.668 --> 00:17:38.289
The fantasy really begins to be something that he thinks,

00:17:38.409 --> 00:17:39.449
I could do this.

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:42.991
For everyone else apart from him,

00:17:43.091 --> 00:17:44.511
it genuinely was a joke because,

00:17:44.671 --> 00:17:44.832
like,

00:17:44.852 --> 00:17:45.872
I know the other guys.

00:17:46.464 --> 00:17:48.085
They did actually really like Becca.

00:17:48.445 --> 00:17:49.426
They thought he was joking,

00:17:49.586 --> 00:17:50.506
that's why it was so funny,

00:17:50.687 --> 00:17:52.628
because it's never going to happen,

00:17:52.668 --> 00:17:53.368
because it's impossible,

00:17:53.369 --> 00:17:54.149
because we all like her.

00:17:56.930 --> 00:18:02.053
Some of Davy's online threats were veiled in text speak and accompanied by emojis.

00:18:03.374 --> 00:18:06.856
Perhaps in case an adult read them and decided to intervene.

00:18:08.137 --> 00:18:11.999
Online conversations are very different to face-to-face conversations.

00:18:13.852 --> 00:18:14.533
If you say,

00:18:15.673 --> 00:18:16.754
I'm going to kill someone,

00:18:17.194 --> 00:18:17.454
lol,

00:18:17.935 --> 00:18:19.036
or smiley face,

00:18:19.696 --> 00:18:23.178
that takes some of the sting out of what's being said,

00:18:23.358 --> 00:18:27.701
especially as the person reading that can't hear your tone of voice,

00:18:28.042 --> 00:18:28.662
can't see your...

00:18:28.742 --> 00:18:45.225
body language doesn't know what you're doing with your face it completely takes any menace out of out of that sentence at all but he also had that serious sight that he was actually planning this without a doubt this was planned we know that from what happened this

00:18:45.265 --> 00:18:57.468
is a psychopath but able to convince his friends he's just a bit of a bully and having a laugh quite incredible we could say that they thought he was joking

00:18:58.196 --> 00:18:59.317
But even joking,

00:18:59.337 --> 00:19:10.641
it shows that we've become so desensitized by social media that these conversations take place and it's almost like they're living this kind of fantasy life that's not real.

00:19:11.142 --> 00:19:14.443
But what they didn't realize is that Joshua wasn't living a fantasy life.

00:19:14.643 --> 00:19:16.304
He was planning to do this in reality.

00:19:21.916 --> 00:19:23.177
After the school year ended,

00:19:23.178 --> 00:19:26.518
the feud between Josh and Rebecca appeared to die down.

00:19:26.858 --> 00:19:30.739
They even hung out together over the summer and rekindled their relationship.

00:19:31.739 --> 00:19:35.260
He may have been telling his friends online that he wanted to kill Rebecca,

00:19:35.640 --> 00:19:38.501
but how does that square with the fact they were getting on so well?

00:19:42.722 --> 00:19:45.183
I'm meeting criminologist Dr Elizabeth Yardley.

00:19:45.715 --> 00:19:50.859
And forensic clinical psychologist Mike Berry to find out what they make of Davies'

00:19:50.899 --> 00:19:51.459
behaviour.

00:19:54.242 --> 00:19:56.123
He was making a threat to kill.

00:19:56.543 --> 00:19:57.164
Kids these days,

00:19:57.224 --> 00:19:57.524
14,

00:19:57.564 --> 00:19:57.824
15,

00:19:58.144 --> 00:20:01.487
they know what a threat to kill is and what that means.

00:20:01.507 --> 00:20:04.129
They've seen enough television programmes about that.

00:20:04.389 --> 00:20:04.509
No,

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:05.290
I disagree with you.

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:08.452
They don't understand the consequences of making a threat.

00:20:08.772 --> 00:20:11.795
So this was make-believe for Joshua's friend.

00:20:12.295 --> 00:20:20.398
I think they would have been reading these comments and chipping in and contributing just with absolutely no idea of the consequences.

00:20:21.159 --> 00:20:24.980
Is he different online to the person he is in real life?

00:20:25.441 --> 00:20:25.701
Yes.

00:20:26.281 --> 00:20:30.703
One thing about the internet is it allows you to be much more yourself.

00:20:30.723 --> 00:20:31.603
It disinhibits.

00:20:31.983 --> 00:20:34.964
It's the effect of alcohol on the frontal lobes.

00:20:35.024 --> 00:20:36.745
When you put somebody in front of a computer,

00:20:37.165 --> 00:20:39.266
they can start being what they want to be.

00:20:39.506 --> 00:20:40.847
They can talk about their fantasies.

00:20:41.395 --> 00:20:44.777
The thing that he really wanted more than anything was control,

00:20:44.977 --> 00:20:46.798
and particularly control over Rebecca.

00:20:47.198 --> 00:20:48.939
And when they lose that control,

00:20:48.999 --> 00:20:50.360
they change the project,

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:51.020
essentially,

00:20:51.321 --> 00:20:52.982
and they don't seek to control them anymore,

00:20:52.983 --> 00:20:54.202
they seek to destroy them.

00:20:56.083 --> 00:21:01.366
I've come to Wales to find out the role social media played in the brutal murder of

00:21:01.746 --> 00:21:07.570
15-year-old Becca Aylward by her ex-boyfriend Joshua Davies in October 2010.

00:21:11.379 --> 00:21:15.281
It was the culmination of a cruel online hate campaign by Davies,

00:21:15.641 --> 00:21:19.624
which began when their three-month romance ended acrimoniously.

00:21:22.745 --> 00:21:23.566
From that moment on,

00:21:23.606 --> 00:21:26.007
he was determined she would never get the better of him,

00:21:26.427 --> 00:21:29.369
and he retaliated by making up lurid rumours online,

00:21:29.709 --> 00:21:32.851
including the fact that he claimed she'd had an abortion.

00:21:33.471 --> 00:21:35.132
When that didn't quieten her down,

00:21:35.492 --> 00:21:40.575
he then started talking more and more about murdering her and trying to rid her from his life.

00:21:41.183 --> 00:21:41.883
Once and for all.

00:21:44.725 --> 00:21:47.346
By the start of the 2010 summer holidays,

00:21:47.667 --> 00:21:51.128
Becca had endured a seven-month hate campaign by Davies.

00:21:51.889 --> 00:21:52.249
But then,

00:21:52.429 --> 00:21:53.010
over the break,

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:55.271
Davies revived their relationship.

00:21:56.191 --> 00:21:59.353
Perhaps Becca hoped they could put all the animosity behind them.

00:22:00.013 --> 00:22:00.674
But in reality,

00:22:01.034 --> 00:22:01.734
for Davies,

00:22:02.134 --> 00:22:04.116
this was all about regaining control.

00:22:05.676 --> 00:22:06.077
Obviously,

00:22:06.157 --> 00:22:08.438
they had rekindled something over the summer,

00:22:08.658 --> 00:22:10.279
but clearly all wasn't well.

00:22:11.195 --> 00:22:18.159
Because she was certainly nervous about going back to school and everything that implied and her complicated relationship with him,

00:22:18.199 --> 00:22:19.780
which wasn't a relationship,

00:22:20.140 --> 00:22:22.481
but he was clearly very much on her mind.

00:22:22.641 --> 00:22:25.923
We know that she was hoping that they might be able to rekindle it,

00:22:25.924 --> 00:22:31.086
but clearly had reservations because she'd said to a school friend that she was nervous about going back.

00:22:36.609 --> 00:22:39.651
Becca mentioned once or twice her worries about going back into Year 11.

00:22:41.075 --> 00:22:43.176
I'd say maybe she had more enemies going into school.

00:22:43.456 --> 00:22:45.097
She was a bit nervous about it.

00:22:47.057 --> 00:22:49.078
One of the last couple of times I spoke to her,

00:22:50.099 --> 00:22:50.679
she just said,

00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:57.062
She just said she didn't think she was going to be alive for too long.

00:23:01.323 --> 00:23:02.744
She always felt threatened.

00:23:04.505 --> 00:23:06.025
I feel like it was related to Josh,

00:23:07.326 --> 00:23:07.766
in my mind,

00:23:07.806 --> 00:23:08.966
100%.

00:23:08.967 --> 00:23:10.027
She hadn't felt like that.

00:23:10.355 --> 00:23:10.835
Like a year ago,

00:23:12.916 --> 00:23:15.117
it was chilling at the time and still is.

00:23:19.339 --> 00:23:20.579
And after the holidays,

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:22.420
following their return to school,

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:28.383
Davies continued his constant dialogue with his friends on social media about killing Becca.

00:23:29.563 --> 00:23:34.265
Josh's mates admitted they were getting quite bored and tired about how much Josh was going on,

00:23:34.665 --> 00:23:37.106
about how much he hated and wanted to kill

00:23:37.567 --> 00:23:37.967
Rebecca.

00:23:38.695 --> 00:23:39.555
One of his best mates,

00:23:39.655 --> 00:23:39.995
Dan,

00:23:40.576 --> 00:23:41.396
told the court,

00:23:41.776 --> 00:23:43.076
you just ignored it.

00:23:43.456 --> 00:23:45.077
It was getting boring,

00:23:45.137 --> 00:23:45.577
he said.

00:23:45.997 --> 00:23:46.857
Perhaps this is why,

00:23:46.917 --> 00:23:49.158
when Josh returned to the subject in science class,

00:23:49.598 --> 00:23:51.199
some of his mates egged him on,

00:23:51.519 --> 00:23:57.660
and one went so far as to make a silly bet with him about what he would do if Josh went ahead with the murder.

00:24:05.543 --> 00:24:06.383
Josh Davidson's friends.

00:24:06.627 --> 00:24:08.549
We meet at a cafe regularly for breakfast.

00:24:09.970 --> 00:24:10.190
Now,

00:24:10.570 --> 00:24:12.672
in one of their conversations where they were talking about,

00:24:13.012 --> 00:24:13.392
once again,

00:24:13.552 --> 00:24:14.073
killing Becca,

00:24:15.534 --> 00:24:16.775
Josh Davis said to one of the people,

00:24:16.775 --> 00:24:17.075
One of them,

00:24:17.855 --> 00:24:20.737
what would you do if I actually did do it?

00:24:21.017 --> 00:24:22.578
And he said,

00:24:22.658 --> 00:24:22.818
oh,

00:24:22.878 --> 00:24:23.938
I'd buy you breakfast.

00:24:28.460 --> 00:24:29.241
It's banal.

00:24:29.421 --> 00:24:31.722
What are you going to do if I really do kill her?

00:24:31.842 --> 00:24:33.242
I'll buy you breakfast.

00:24:33.543 --> 00:24:35.283
That is not menacing.

00:24:35.383 --> 00:24:37.844
That's bringing it back into the real world.

00:24:39.205 --> 00:24:41.146
Turns it into a joke almost for them,

00:24:41.906 --> 00:24:42.767
but not for him.

00:24:46.963 --> 00:24:55.187
I think that shows what element of boredom his peer group had with Davis and his continual vendetta against Rebecca.

00:24:55.747 --> 00:24:58.049
It clearly wasn't a serious monetary amount.

00:24:58.449 --> 00:25:00.210
It wasn't an impossible bet,

00:25:00.290 --> 00:25:00.630
such as,

00:25:00.790 --> 00:25:02.171
I would bet you a million dollars,

00:25:02.191 --> 00:25:02.331
which,

00:25:02.332 --> 00:25:02.711
of course,

00:25:03.091 --> 00:25:03.832
is impossible.

00:25:04.352 --> 00:25:10.435
This just showed the boredom and disdain I think his peer group had for this constant vendetta.

00:25:22.906 --> 00:25:24.386
Just two days before the murder,

00:25:24.647 --> 00:25:26.027
Josh texted a friend.

00:25:27.048 --> 00:25:28.049
And don't say anything,

00:25:28.189 --> 00:25:29.850
but you may just owe me breakfast,

00:25:29.851 --> 00:25:30.230
he said,

00:25:30.690 --> 00:25:37.494
referring to a bet he'd made with Liam that Liam would have to pay for breakfast at this cafe if he went ahead with the murder.

00:25:38.254 --> 00:25:39.115
Liam responded,

00:25:39.455 --> 00:25:41.176
best text I've ever had,

00:25:41.256 --> 00:25:41.536
mate.

00:25:41.776 --> 00:25:42.377
If it's true,

00:25:42.577 --> 00:25:44.338
I'm happy to pay for your breakfast.

00:25:45.078 --> 00:25:45.939
Josh responded...

00:25:46.179 --> 00:25:46.319
Well,

00:25:46.359 --> 00:25:48.901
hopefully by Friday it will all be done and dusted.

00:25:49.802 --> 00:25:50.522
Revving him up,

00:25:50.702 --> 00:25:51.603
Liam responded,

00:25:51.983 --> 00:25:53.884
I'll hear all the details Saturday,

00:25:54.245 --> 00:25:55.505
sadistic bastard.

00:25:56.406 --> 00:25:56.546
Well,

00:25:56.547 --> 00:26:00.049
it seems that Josh's plans to murder Rebecca were well in motion.

00:26:00.409 --> 00:26:02.670
But why was his friend playing on with it?

00:26:02.890 --> 00:26:04.912
Did he not realise he was encouraging him?

00:26:08.514 --> 00:26:14.018
The state of mind that Davis is now in is that the plan to murder Rebecca has started.

00:26:16.351 --> 00:26:17.853
The message was part of the process.

00:26:18.674 --> 00:26:24.281
It is an awful shame that the friend didn't just suddenly realise what a dangerous person

00:26:24.962 --> 00:26:25.923
Davis was.

00:26:43.203 --> 00:26:45.565
On the 23rd of October 2010,

00:26:45.585 --> 00:26:48.367
on the first weekend of the school half-term,

00:26:48.928 --> 00:26:51.070
Davies invited Rebecca to meet him here,

00:26:51.510 --> 00:26:52.451
close to his home.

00:26:52.971 --> 00:26:54.673
And given her soft spot for him,

00:26:55.113 --> 00:26:57.415
despite all the rumours he'd spread about her,

00:26:57.975 --> 00:26:58.876
Rebecca agreed.

00:27:03.940 --> 00:27:06.683
After a ten-month war of words with Davies,

00:27:07.103 --> 00:27:11.246
Becca must have felt relieved that her nightmare seemed finally to be over.

00:27:12.443 --> 00:27:15.044
Having spoken to him the night before and made all their arrangements,

00:27:15.104 --> 00:27:16.745
Becca was obviously really excited,

00:27:17.566 --> 00:27:18.967
up very early in the morning.

00:27:19.927 --> 00:27:21.848
She'd chosen her clothes really carefully,

00:27:22.268 --> 00:27:23.529
she'd painted her nails,

00:27:23.589 --> 00:27:25.650
she'd done her hair really carefully,

00:27:26.811 --> 00:27:28.051
put on a bit of make-up.

00:27:29.172 --> 00:27:31.954
Basically done everything she could to make herself beautiful for him.

00:27:34.015 --> 00:27:34.475
Hoping,

00:27:34.715 --> 00:27:38.137
hoping this was the moment when they were going to get back together,

00:27:38.138 --> 00:27:39.257
when everything was going to be OK.

00:27:47.923 --> 00:27:50.164
There was romance in the air as far as she was concerned,

00:27:51.145 --> 00:27:53.426
not violence and certainly not murder.

00:28:07.112 --> 00:28:08.373
For Joshua Davies,

00:28:08.773 --> 00:28:12.735
this was to be the climax of his deadly battle for control over Becca.

00:28:14.003 --> 00:28:17.746
While Josh hung out with his friends Liam and Daniel here at Daniel's house,

00:28:18.006 --> 00:28:21.068
Rebecca called to say she was ready and will be there soon.

00:28:21.668 --> 00:28:23.129
As soon as Josh hung up the phone,

00:28:23.309 --> 00:28:24.410
in a sing-along voice,

00:28:24.590 --> 00:28:25.451
he started singing,

00:28:25.771 --> 00:28:26.832
Today's the day.

00:28:27.272 --> 00:28:28.873
He explicitly told his friends...

00:28:29.173 --> 00:28:32.416
He was going to meet Rebecca and then he was going to kill her.

00:28:32.917 --> 00:28:36.661
He said he'd be back soon because he didn't think it would take too long.

00:28:37.602 --> 00:28:40.965
Why on earth didn't Liam and Daniel take him seriously?

00:28:41.525 --> 00:28:43.467
Why didn't they take him at his word?

00:28:50.591 --> 00:28:58.457
Clearly he's getting very excited about what he's going to do because this is something that he has been looking forward to.

00:29:01.379 --> 00:29:06.583
I think his friends must have suspected he was going to hurt her and he was going to bully her,

00:29:07.264 --> 00:29:09.646
but I don't think they thought he was going to kill her.

00:29:24.299 --> 00:29:26.800
Becca arrived at the meeting point as arranged,

00:29:27.300 --> 00:29:30.081
but with no sign of Davies and worried he'd stood her up,

00:29:30.501 --> 00:29:31.361
she called her mother,

00:29:31.461 --> 00:29:31.801
Sonia.

00:29:32.841 --> 00:29:36.302
But then Becca spotted Davies coming to meet her and ended the call,

00:29:36.522 --> 00:29:39.203
saying goodbye to her mother for the very last time.

00:29:40.383 --> 00:29:42.284
He takes her up to Pennsylvania Woods,

00:29:42.924 --> 00:29:46.125
which is a spot where a lot of the local kids would go and hang out.

00:29:47.285 --> 00:29:47.485
Though,

00:29:47.565 --> 00:29:48.406
as Sonia said,

00:29:48.826 --> 00:29:51.547
not a place Becca would have ever hung out.

00:29:53.543 --> 00:29:55.825
She wasn't the sort of girl who'd go tramping through the woods.

00:29:56.765 --> 00:30:00.248
It remains a mystery why she went up with him willingly.

00:30:03.230 --> 00:30:03.911
We'll never know.

00:30:21.823 --> 00:30:23.404
Soon after entering the woods,

00:30:23.784 --> 00:30:25.185
Davies turned on Becca.

00:30:32.909 --> 00:30:33.289
First,

00:30:33.469 --> 00:30:34.970
he tried to break her neck.

00:30:42.559 --> 00:30:43.680
But when that failed,

00:30:43.940 --> 00:30:45.561
he grabbed a large rock.

00:30:51.465 --> 00:30:53.146
And bludgeoned Beckett to death.

00:31:15.795 --> 00:31:18.237
The murder was brutal,

00:31:18.837 --> 00:31:23.421
far more violence than was necessary to just kill Rebecca.

00:31:25.742 --> 00:31:28.785
I think that he enjoyed hurting her.

00:31:33.968 --> 00:31:38.312
That would have been the most distressing and horrific sight to see.

00:31:39.132 --> 00:31:40.833
And yet he coolly does it.

00:31:41.474 --> 00:31:42.114
And then...

00:31:43.579 --> 00:31:43.699
So,

00:31:44.500 --> 00:31:46.281
so calculating.

00:31:46.721 --> 00:31:48.142
When his friend says,

00:31:48.522 --> 00:31:49.162
are you with

00:31:49.622 --> 00:31:51.403
Rebecca? He replies,

00:31:51.503 --> 00:31:52.404
define with.

00:31:54.705 --> 00:31:57.526
That comment makes the hers stand up on the back of your neck.

00:31:59.075 --> 00:32:00.516
She had no idea it was coming,

00:32:00.536 --> 00:32:03.336
which probably in a lot of ways is a blessing.

00:32:03.837 --> 00:32:09.679
It would be worse if she had lots of defensive wounds and knew exactly what was happening to her,

00:32:09.739 --> 00:32:17.441
so we can take maybe some blessing from the fact that she probably died quite quickly not knowing what was happening.

00:32:26.555 --> 00:32:31.937
I wonder if Davies had planned to murder Becca from the moment his social media vendetta began.

00:32:32.857 --> 00:32:37.258
Criminologist Dr Liz Yardley and psychologist Mike Berry might have the answer.

00:32:37.978 --> 00:32:39.819
Is Joshua a psychopath?

00:32:40.299 --> 00:32:40.439
Well,

00:32:40.519 --> 00:32:44.120
he's somebody who does display some psychopathic traits and behaviours,

00:32:44.180 --> 00:32:44.560
I think.

00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:46.521
So there's a lack of remorse,

00:32:46.581 --> 00:32:47.681
there's a lack of empathy.

00:32:47.841 --> 00:32:51.162
there's a failure to accept responsibility for his own actions.

00:32:51.422 --> 00:32:53.083
There's a manipulativeness about him.

00:32:53.783 --> 00:32:54.624
I disagree with you.

00:32:55.064 --> 00:32:59.405
I don't think there's anything in his history to suggest that he was psychopathic.

00:32:59.505 --> 00:33:00.146
Control,

00:33:00.406 --> 00:33:01.106
narcissism,

00:33:01.766 --> 00:33:02.667
lack of remorse,

00:33:02.887 --> 00:33:03.687
manipulation,

00:33:03.787 --> 00:33:04.687
kind of bullying,

00:33:05.067 --> 00:33:06.708
humiliations upon his friends.

00:33:06.748 --> 00:33:08.909
No history of any antisocial behaviour,

00:33:08.989 --> 00:33:13.050
no history of criminality that we would expect to see in a

00:33:13.390 --> 00:33:14.351
16-year-old psychopath.

00:33:15.155 --> 00:33:17.757
I suppose I think of psychopathy as a spectrum.

00:33:18.457 --> 00:33:19.478
At one extreme end,

00:33:19.758 --> 00:33:22.600
you have got people who are undoubtedly psychopaths,

00:33:22.620 --> 00:33:23.120
at the other end,

00:33:23.160 --> 00:33:24.421
people who absolutely aren't.

00:33:24.781 --> 00:33:27.963
And I do think he is kind of occupying this middle ground here.

00:33:28.303 --> 00:33:32.865
But what we really need to remember here is that he knew exactly what he was doing when he killed her.

00:33:33.145 --> 00:33:34.506
He knew what he was doing was wrong.

00:33:35.166 --> 00:33:40.868
So let's not kind of labour under the impression that he was out of his mind or that he wasn't responsible for this.

00:33:41.128 --> 00:33:44.150
When we look at the fact that he doesn't have a history of violence,

00:33:44.210 --> 00:33:44.890
many people think,

00:33:44.930 --> 00:33:45.330
well,

00:33:45.350 --> 00:33:46.251
that's really shocking.

00:33:46.252 --> 00:33:49.572
He literally turns overnight from this average schoolboy into this killer.

00:33:49.952 --> 00:33:54.714
But actually what he has got a history of is controlling and jealous and possessive behaviour.

00:33:55.254 --> 00:33:56.835
That is the biggest risk factor.

00:33:59.675 --> 00:34:00.937
In 2010,

00:34:01.217 --> 00:34:08.005
the village of Abercanvig in Wales was shocked by the brutal murder of a teenage girl by her ex-boyfriend,

00:34:08.405 --> 00:34:11.168
following months of vicious threats on social media.

00:34:12.330 --> 00:34:12.930
This is where

00:34:13.371 --> 00:34:16.675
15-year-old Rebecca Aylward took her final steps.

00:34:17.055 --> 00:34:20.196
She was invited up here by her ex-boyfriend,

00:34:20.657 --> 00:34:21.737
Joshua Davies.

00:34:22.097 --> 00:34:24.098
She thought he was going to ask her out again.

00:34:24.218 --> 00:34:24.698
Instead,

00:34:24.978 --> 00:34:29.540
he battered her head in with a stone and left her lying face down in the ground.

00:34:30.601 --> 00:34:32.161
Joshua then texted his friends,

00:34:32.242 --> 00:34:32.982
Liam and Daniel,

00:34:33.242 --> 00:34:35.983
and asked them to meet him up here in the forest.

00:34:36.323 --> 00:34:38.484
But Liam had a bad leg and was left behind.

00:34:38.764 --> 00:34:41.926
But when Daniel arrived here and connected with Joshua,

00:34:42.206 --> 00:34:44.987
he saw Rebecca lying on the ground and immediately...

00:34:45.267 --> 00:34:46.608
realized what had happened.

00:34:48.108 --> 00:34:50.189
Joshua had done what he said he'd do.

00:35:00.634 --> 00:35:05.256
He called his friends up to see the body because he was proud of what he'd done.

00:35:05.676 --> 00:35:11.018
He'd actually gone through with what he said he was going to do and he thought that when his friends saw that,

00:35:11.258 --> 00:35:11.958
he'd be the hero.

00:35:15.255 --> 00:35:18.776
Daniel claimed that when he saw Rebecca's body lying on the floor,

00:35:18.876 --> 00:35:21.737
he said it felt like he'd walked into a cold shower.

00:35:21.817 --> 00:35:23.257
He suddenly felt numb,

00:35:23.717 --> 00:35:25.618
he felt very dizzy and shuddery,

00:35:26.058 --> 00:35:27.258
and it didn't seem real.

00:35:27.898 --> 00:35:30.099
And he immediately wanted to get away from there.

00:35:32.100 --> 00:35:33.660
Davis was completely different.

00:35:34.380 --> 00:35:37.501
He seemed to be more concerned that he didn't have any blood on himself.

00:35:37.961 --> 00:35:42.442
So already he was thinking about getting his way out of this situation.

00:35:43.623 --> 00:35:44.723
Davis then tells him...

00:35:45.171 --> 00:35:50.495
That he's killed her by hitting her with a rock and that he had to kill her with a rock because she wouldn't stop screaming.

00:35:51.276 --> 00:35:58.302
He says that he's tried to kill her by strangling her and also getting her in a neck hold,

00:35:58.382 --> 00:35:59.423
as he put it,

00:35:59.583 --> 00:36:00.804
but that it was too difficult.

00:36:01.724 --> 00:36:05.608
And apparently he relates all this to Daniel with absolutely no emotion,

00:36:06.208 --> 00:36:06.929
no remorse,

00:36:07.309 --> 00:36:07.669
nothing.

00:36:12.693 --> 00:36:14.595
Davies and Daniel left the forest.

00:36:14.959 --> 00:36:17.480
met up with Liam and went to Daniel's house.

00:36:18.761 --> 00:36:22.682
Davies told Liam to delete all his messages from that day and said,

00:36:23.363 --> 00:36:24.183
if anyone asks,

00:36:24.583 --> 00:36:26.384
I've been here with you all the time.

00:36:28.305 --> 00:36:29.985
Liam agreed to keep his secret.

00:36:31.346 --> 00:36:33.547
Davies does what most offenders will try and do,

00:36:33.907 --> 00:36:35.748
which is to cover their tracks.

00:36:36.708 --> 00:36:40.210
This is suddenly the classic case of not understanding technology,

00:36:40.450 --> 00:36:40.990
messaging,

00:36:41.510 --> 00:36:42.711
thinking if you delete them,

00:36:42.991 --> 00:36:43.451
they've gone.

00:36:43.711 --> 00:36:44.992
we know that they haven't gone.

00:36:45.933 --> 00:36:46.353
Davies'

00:36:46.393 --> 00:36:48.155
friends agreed to be his alibi.

00:36:48.675 --> 00:36:50.837
He then went online to back up his story,

00:36:51.418 --> 00:36:52.259
saying on Facebook,

00:36:52.819 --> 00:36:55.642
Joshua D is still chilling with Liam and Daniel.

00:36:56.622 --> 00:37:00.566
Davies even referred obliquely to a playful bet from one of his friends,

00:37:00.846 --> 00:37:03.629
offering him a free breakfast if he killed Becca.

00:37:05.971 --> 00:37:10.615
The next behaviours we see from Davies are him laying the groundwork of his alibis.

00:37:11.251 --> 00:37:15.193
Posting on social media that he'd been relaxing all day watching videos,

00:37:16.293 --> 00:37:19.855
providing this very dark joke about having had a great breakfast that day.

00:37:20.355 --> 00:37:20.675
Again,

00:37:20.735 --> 00:37:25.937
this just shows the amount of disregard he had for human life by making that very sick joke.

00:37:28.198 --> 00:37:28.998
Later that day,

00:37:29.318 --> 00:37:30.919
when Becca didn't return home,

00:37:31.239 --> 00:37:34.120
her mom rang Davies and asked him where she was.

00:37:35.421 --> 00:37:40.223
He said they hadn't met up in the end and he thought she'd gone to see a different Josh instead.

00:37:43.205 --> 00:38:03.799
Becca couldn't be located and as news of her disappearance spread her friends started messaging each other online chillingly the person who knew exactly where she was joined in he

00:38:04.199 --> 00:38:09.063
is just basically calmly going through the process of covering his tracks

00:38:10.151 --> 00:38:17.497
Making sure that everybody is looking elsewhere.

00:38:17.498 --> 00:38:18.498
He probably wants to run,

00:38:19.158 --> 00:38:20.840
he probably wants to get as far away as possible,

00:38:20.860 --> 00:38:22.901
but he can't do that because that shows guilt.

00:38:23.562 --> 00:38:24.403
So he's in a quandary,

00:38:24.423 --> 00:38:27.125
so you've got a bit of chaotic behaviour going on here,

00:38:27.365 --> 00:38:28.666
but he's doing bits of everything.

00:38:29.046 --> 00:38:30.287
He's trying to control his friends,

00:38:30.288 --> 00:38:31.468
he's trying to control evidence,

00:38:31.488 --> 00:38:35.812
but he's also trying to be this wonderful person that school and friends think he is,

00:38:35.813 --> 00:38:36.853
this wonderful great guy,

00:38:37.373 --> 00:38:38.134
but he can't be both.

00:38:38.135 --> 00:38:39.635
And he...

00:38:39.855 --> 00:38:42.317
probably thought he was being quite clever,

00:38:42.377 --> 00:38:45.579
and with the kind of narcissistic personality that he had,

00:38:46.379 --> 00:38:51.743
he wouldn't even have considered that he wasn't cleverer than everybody else.

00:38:54.045 --> 00:38:58.067
There will always be an element of naivety in most offended behaviour.

00:38:58.668 --> 00:39:01.350
Did he really believe he could get away with murder?

00:39:03.871 --> 00:39:05.552
He's trying to get rid of his digital footprint,

00:39:05.933 --> 00:39:09.335
but he's actually shown and admitted murder to a friend by showing...

00:39:09.663 --> 00:39:16.635
then the body how does that work so in many ways it's this control

00:39:16.775 --> 00:39:18.156
He was proud of what he did,

00:39:18.917 --> 00:39:19.858
but in the other aspect,

00:39:20.218 --> 00:39:23.000
naive in that he felt he wanted to get away with it,

00:39:23.561 --> 00:39:24.021
but he couldn't.

00:39:24.762 --> 00:39:25.802
So there is naivety,

00:39:26.183 --> 00:39:28.324
but there's also pride in what he actually achieved.

00:39:28.384 --> 00:39:29.545
That's very dangerous.

00:39:34.109 --> 00:39:39.013
Despite Davey's attempts to cover his tracks online and delete various text messages,

00:39:39.313 --> 00:39:40.995
the net was already closing in.

00:39:41.515 --> 00:39:41.635
By

00:39:42.796 --> 00:39:44.878
7.45am, Liam had already cracked,

00:39:45.238 --> 00:39:46.059
telling his parents...

00:39:46.379 --> 00:39:47.900
everything he knew about the murder.

00:39:48.780 --> 00:39:49.360
Shortly after,

00:39:49.420 --> 00:39:50.421
the police arrested

00:39:50.861 --> 00:39:55.343
Josh, Liam and Daniel and brought them here to Cardiff Bay Police Station.

00:39:55.783 --> 00:39:57.664
But Davies still brazened it out.

00:39:57.924 --> 00:39:58.844
He told the police that,

00:39:58.924 --> 00:39:59.165
yes,

00:39:59.525 --> 00:40:00.845
Rebecca was murdered,

00:40:01.125 --> 00:40:02.046
but he didn't do it.

00:40:02.446 --> 00:40:03.727
He blamed his best friend,

00:40:03.827 --> 00:40:04.207
Daniel.

00:40:10.589 --> 00:40:12.010
One of the other things I find really,

00:40:12.390 --> 00:40:13.651
really shocking is the...

00:40:14.339 --> 00:40:19.381
Ease with which he apparently decided he'd fit up his supposed best friend.

00:40:21.702 --> 00:40:24.903
It almost beggars belief that he thought that anybody would possibly believe him.

00:40:27.324 --> 00:40:37.668
He wouldn't have thought twice about blaming somebody else and he would have been very happy to see that person go to prison probably for it with no remorse whatsoever.

00:40:42.811 --> 00:40:43.791
Throughout the trial...

00:40:44.135 --> 00:40:50.078
Davies protested his innocence and constantly blamed his best friend Daniel for Becca's murder.

00:40:51.398 --> 00:40:57.361
But the jury found Davies guilty and he was jailed for life with a minimum of 14 years.

00:41:09.646 --> 00:41:11.207
At trial he appeared to be distant.

00:41:12.251 --> 00:41:14.012
As if he had no interest in his own trial,

00:41:14.772 --> 00:41:15.553
in his own future.

00:41:16.253 --> 00:41:17.294
I think at that age,

00:41:17.794 --> 00:41:21.336
it should be terrifying to be told that if you're found guilty,

00:41:21.656 --> 00:41:23.697
the sentence will have to be one of life imprisonment.

00:41:24.738 --> 00:41:25.778
To a boy of that age,

00:41:26.199 --> 00:41:27.259
no more girlfriends,

00:41:27.319 --> 00:41:28.140
no university,

00:41:28.420 --> 00:41:29.020
no freedom,

00:41:29.840 --> 00:41:30.961
for who knows how many years,

00:41:31.902 --> 00:41:32.902
but he showed no reaction.

00:41:34.663 --> 00:41:35.624
As a criminologist,

00:41:35.845 --> 00:41:39.650
I know it's possible to group online killers into different categories,

00:41:40.071 --> 00:41:40.892
such as predator,

00:41:41.252 --> 00:41:42.754
imposter or reactor.

00:41:43.435 --> 00:41:49.824
I'm meeting experts Dr Liz Yardley and psychologist Mike Berry to find out what sort of social media murderer

00:41:50.245 --> 00:41:50.986
Davies was.

00:41:52.131 --> 00:41:52.291
Liz,

00:41:52.591 --> 00:41:54.192
what kind of killer was Davies?

00:41:54.612 --> 00:41:54.732
Well,

00:41:54.852 --> 00:41:59.134
I'd describe Davies as an informer type of killer who uses social media.

00:41:59.554 --> 00:42:05.216
And this is the type of person who will use social media to communicate an intention to kill somebody,

00:42:05.916 --> 00:42:09.738
to inform their social media followers that they have just killed someone,

00:42:10.018 --> 00:42:10.478
or both.

00:42:10.498 --> 00:42:12.699
So they're using it as a communicative tool.

00:42:12.899 --> 00:42:13.540
around murder.

00:42:14.040 --> 00:42:18.184
Why was he so keen to tell everybody what he was going to do if he didn't care what they thought?

00:42:18.765 --> 00:42:18.905
Well,

00:42:18.965 --> 00:42:21.107
I think for him it was a performance,

00:42:21.147 --> 00:42:21.688
essentially.

00:42:21.908 --> 00:42:24.050
It was asserting power,

00:42:24.270 --> 00:42:28.695
because he felt that he'd lost quite a lot of control in that relationship with Rebecca.

00:42:29.115 --> 00:42:32.118
But here was a way of having a new kind of status,

00:42:32.138 --> 00:42:33.219
a new identity.

00:42:33.820 --> 00:42:36.503
So I think that was something that he gained quite a lot of pleasure from.

00:42:36.943 --> 00:42:38.144
Without social media,

00:42:38.244 --> 00:42:40.345
do you think Rebecca would still be alive today?

00:42:40.605 --> 00:42:48.009
I think there's a possibility without it that after a couple of months they would have broken up from school and they would have gone their separate ways.

00:42:48.409 --> 00:42:53.432
So in many ways the internet kept the fire going and sped up the whole process.

00:42:54.713 --> 00:42:57.334
What caused these murderous thoughts in the first place?

00:42:58.895 --> 00:43:02.057
I think he didn't like being out of control.

00:43:02.097 --> 00:43:06.039
I think he didn't like the threat that had to his ego.

00:43:06.519 --> 00:43:10.542
to have somebody in control of things when he wants to be in control.

00:43:10.582 --> 00:43:10.982
Liz,

00:43:11.402 --> 00:43:13.344
how could this tragedy have been avoided?

00:43:13.984 --> 00:43:17.847
I think the key thing that we need to be looking at here isn't necessarily social media,

00:43:18.147 --> 00:43:21.569
but young people's relationships and the nature of those relationships.

00:43:21.970 --> 00:43:22.090
Now,

00:43:22.130 --> 00:43:25.932
teenagers do tend to be quite intense in terms of their emotions,

00:43:26.212 --> 00:43:32.016
but when you see the kind of controlling and jealous and possessive behaviour that Dave has exhibited towards Rebecca,

00:43:32.457 --> 00:43:33.878
that's a cause for concern for me,

00:43:33.918 --> 00:43:35.819
and that's where we need to educate young people.

00:43:35.979 --> 00:43:37.240
But it's that intensity,

00:43:37.660 --> 00:43:40.602
that pressure cooker that social media can sometimes become,

00:43:40.822 --> 00:43:42.883
has played quite a large role in this case.

00:43:46.225 --> 00:43:55.210
The unreal world of social media created an environment where a bright young teenager literally talked himself into the act of murder.

00:43:55.971 --> 00:43:59.332
Online threats are no less real than the spoken word.

00:43:59.733 --> 00:44:00.753
And in this instance,

00:44:01.113 --> 00:44:03.535
led to a needless and tragic murder.

